{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>חבור</b> — some say:" "<b>כי עצבים</b> — like: וכל עצביכם (and all your idols). And the correct interpretation: like העצב נבזה (the despised idol) — the idols of Canaan, and all from the root עצבון (grief/pain), for there is no benefit in their fetishes, only pain. And the meaning: they are joined to the fetishes — they are their companions." "<b>הנח לו</b> — until He removes him; perhaps their eyes will be opened."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:50:08.797982429Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}